      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this would work. Straightforwardly turning this check into a guard clause would make the timeout check below unreachable. Switching the ordering and turning the timeout check into a guard clause would cause a chunk that arrived right at the deadline to be treated as an error rather than a successful reception. In the rest of the TCPM, we check the received flag first and then the timeout to avoid an error in this marginal case.",
